  <h2 id="playground-host-slot" class="sr-only">Playground host screenshot slot</h2>
  {% set slotKind = "screenshot" %}
  {% set slotLabel = "Playground shell with iframe app" %}
  {% set slotHint = "16:9 · host chrome around a real app. Not a generated mock." %}
  {% set slotRatio = "video" %}
  {% include "media-slot.njk" %}
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="layout-modes">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="layout-modes" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Layout is a shell concern</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Pick <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">layout</code> in <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.config.json</code>. Every microfrontend inherits it. App UI must work in sidebar, app-bar, and windows. Default is <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">sidebar</code>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 md:grid-cols-3 md:gap-6 lg:gap-8">
    <div>
      {% set layoutMode = "sidebar" %}
      {% include "shell-layout-anim.njk" %}
      <h3 class="mt-5 text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Sidebar</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Persistent navigation beside the iframe. Also <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">sidebar-inset</code> for a padded main frame.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      {% set layoutMode = "topbar" %}
      {% include "shell-layout-anim.njk" %}
      <h3 class="mt-5 text-base font-semibold text-foreground">App bar</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground"><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">app-bar</code> and <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">app-bar-inset</code> move navigation to a compact top bar.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      {% set layoutMode = "window" %}
      {% include "shell-layout-anim.njk" %}
      <h3 class="mt-5 text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Windows</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground"><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">windows</code> is a proof of concept: taskbar, start menu, one window per nav item. Not recommended for production.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground"><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">floating</code> is glass chrome over full-bleed content. <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">fullscreen</code> hides nav chrome. Size iframe UI to 100% of the iframe, not <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">100vh</code>.</p>
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="sdk-chrome">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="sdk-chrome" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Toasts, dialogs, and theme from the SDK</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">The shell already owns toasts, dialogs, modals, drawers, theme, and language. From the iframe you call them on <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui</code> after <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">init</code> - no extra overlay stack in your app. Theme pickers, locale switchers, and floating actions are in <a class="font-medium text-primary-ink underline underline-offset-2 dark:text-primary" href="#host-chrome">host chrome</a>.</p>
  </div>
  {% include "shell-sdk-examples.njk" %}
</section>

<section id="host-chrome" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="host-chrome-heading">
  <div class="grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 id="host-chrome-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Theme, language, and floating actions</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">The host already draws the sidebar or app bar, toasts, dialogs, drawers, and the account menu. Theme, language, and floating actions belong there too. Your iframe reads settings and declares intent. Do not ship a second theme picker or locale switcher unless that iframe is the settings surface.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">JS starters from <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui init</code> call <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.applyTheme()</code> and listen for language with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">@shellui/sdk/tiny</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      {% include "feature-visual-chrome.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-16" aria-labelledby="theme-screenshot-slot">
  <h2 id="theme-screenshot-slot" class="sr-only">Theme settings screenshot slot</h2>
  {% set slotKind = "screenshot" %}
  {% set slotLabel = "Settings Appearance theme picker" %}
  {% set slotHint = "16:9 · playground Settings. Not a generated mock." %}
  {% set slotRatio = "video" %}
  {% include "media-slot.njk" %}
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="theming">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="theming" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Themes in config, not in the iframe</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Theming follows the shadcn/ui CSS variable model. Tokens are full CSS colors. Prefer OKLCH. There is no live theme editor. Configuration lives in <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.config.json</code> or JSON under <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">themesDir</code>.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground"><code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui init</code> sets the official palette with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">"theme": "shellui"</code>. <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">@shellui/core</code> ships curated JSON themes (47, including Shellui, shadcn, and tweakcn palettes). Settings → Appearance scales with how many you enable.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
    {% highlight "json", "shellui.config.json" %}
{
  "theme": "shellui",
  "themes": ["shellui", "claude", "shadcn"],
  "activeTheme": "shellui"
}
    {% endhighlight %}
  </div>
  <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-sm/6 text-muted-foreground">Read <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">settings.appearance</code> from the SDK. Inline objects and a <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.8rem]">themesDir</code> folder are documented in the themes guide.</p>
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="language">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="language" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Language is a shell setting</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Set <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">language</code> to one code or an array. Built-in UI strings exist for English (<code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">en</code>) and French (<code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">fr</code>). Users change the active language in Settings → Language.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Navigation labels, group titles, administration copy, and cookie-consent text accept a string or a <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">LocalizedString</code> object. Iframe apps should listen for SDK language / <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">SHELLUI_SETTINGS</code> and update their own copy. Layouts are LTR.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
    {% highlight "json", "shellui.config.json" %}
{
  "language": ["en", "fr"]
}
    {% endhighlight %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="chrome-actions">
  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <h2 id="chrome-actions" class="scroll-mt-24 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-3xl">Floating actions from the SDK</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">Apps declare optional back, title, trailing, and primary floating action chrome with <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">shellui.actions.set</code>. The shell renders them, reserves safe padding, and posts <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">SHELLUI_ACTION</code> clicks into that iframe only. Caps: at most 3 trailing visible on desktop (rest in an overflow menu), at most 1 primary.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-muted-foreground">The shell does not infer actions from the iframe URL. On every in-app route change, call <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">set</code> or <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm">clear</code>. Navigating the shell to another app clears that iframe's actions.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl">
    {% highlight "ts", "app.ts" %}
import { shellui } from "@shellui/sdk";

await shellui.init();

shellui.actions.set({
  back: { id: "back", onClick: () => history.back() },
  title: "Inbox",
  trailing: [
    { id: "edit", label: "Edit", onClick: () => {} },
  ],
  primary: { id: "compose", icon: "plus", onClick: () => {} },
});
    {% endhighlight %}
  </div>
  <div class="mt-10">
    {% set slotKind = "screenshot" %}
    {% set slotLabel = "Chrome actions over an iframe" %}
    {% set slotHint = "16:9 · trailing actions and primary floating action. Not a generated mock." %}
    {% set slotRatio = "video" %}
    {% include "media-slot.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>

